{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והיה כי יביאך", :translit "vehayah ki yevi'akha", :gloss "and it shall be when He brings you"} {:he "שמע", :translit "shema", :gloss "hear"} {:he "תורה", :translit "torah", :gloss "Torah"} {:he "תפילין", :translit "tefillin", :gloss "phylacteries"} {:he "מזוזה", :translit "mezuzah", :gloss "doorpost-scroll"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (סמך): the phrase 'and it shall be, when He brings you' immediately follows the Shema passage, signaling a causal link — entry to the Land is earned through the mitzvot just mentioned."}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim observes that the promise 'when He brings you into the Land' (Deuteronomy 6:10) directly follows the Shema paragraph (Deuteronomy 6:4–9), which contains the commandments of Torah study, tefillin, and mezuzah. The lesson drawn from this juxtaposition is that inheritance of the Land is contingent on the merit of these mitzvot. This builds on the broader principle that the Land was given on condition of Israel's commitment to Torah, as stated at Leviticus 26:3–12 and developed at Sifrei Devarim 43.", :sources ["Leviticus 26:3–12" "Sifrei Devarim 43"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (סמך): the phrase 'and it shall be, when He brings you' immediately follows the Shema passage, signaling a causal link — entry to the Land is earned through the mitzvot just mentioned.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:48.715602111Z", :model "glm-5.2"}